      },
      "worked": "For $a,b,c>0$ with $a,b,c\\ne1$, change all logarithms to base $a$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\log_a(b)\\times\\log_b(c)\\times\\log_c(a)&=\\log_a(b)\\times\\frac{\\log_a(c)}{\\log_a(b)}\\times\\frac{\\log_a(a)}{\\log_a(c)}\\\\\\log_a(b)\\times\\log_b(c)\\times\\log_c(a)&=\\log_a(a)\\\\\\log_a(b)\\times\\log_b(c)\\times\\log_c(a)&=1.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
